{"name":"Blossom Blue","hex":"#aaccee","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in spring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png/330px-Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom","wikidata":"Q2047589"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/500px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/1280px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/500px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cherry blossoms, Paris, full bloom","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Orange_Blossom.JPG/500px-Orange_Blossom.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Orange_Blossom.JPG/1280px-Orange_Blossom.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Orange_Blossom.JPG/500px-Orange_Blossom.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orange blossom","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrange_Blossom.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/MeihuaShan_1.jpg/500px-MeihuaShan_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Mei